Definition:
    -The Facade pattern is a structural design pattern where there is high level interface for a set
     of complex subsystem interfaces

How is it done:
    -Using the concept of dependency injection and loosely coupling required classes and interfaces and providing
     a single interface that delegates the work


Why Facade Pattern:
    -Facade pattern is basically used for reducing complexity on the client side, the client using the features
     doesn't have to work with any of the complex implementation but only a simple api provided by the pattern

